{
  "id": 19,
  "name": "centrality_aware_v1",
  "intent": "Extends parent's nonlinear lookahead by adding a mean_remaining penalty that prefers candidates whose average distance to other unvisited nodes is small (central candidates), which discourages the early detour toward peripheral nodes that hurt uniform and grid tours. A small cluster_density bonus preserves the parent's strong clustered performance. The parent's urgency lookahead (nr/(d+0.1)), progress-superlinear regret weight, and return penalty are retained unchanged as the validated backbone, so NN structure still dominates.",
  "tags": [
    "nonlinear",
    "lookahead"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    r = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    mr = f['mean_remaining']\n    p15 = p ** 1.5\n    weight_regret = 0.15 + 0.25 * p15\n    term1 = -d\n    term2 = 0.05 * nr / (d + 0.1 + 1e-9)\n    term3 = weight_regret * r\n    term4 = 0.30 * rd * (1 + 0.5 * p)\n    term5 = -0.04 * mr\n    term6 = 0.02 * cd\n    s = term1 + term2 + term3 + term4 + term5 + term6\n    return s",
  "source": "live_llm",
